# Weekly gate run on each machine that runs lane-run (system sd:5986):
# `machine-setup.sh doctor gate` runs `make check` in the system checkout,
# then in the pack, each in the machine's gate queue (`sd gate run
# --max-wait 3600`). A pass or a real failure is the verdict the hub-ready
# block reads on a failover standby; a slot timeout (exit 75) or a run
# killed before its verdict records none, and hub-ready notes it from this
# job's stamp. Any exit but 0 files a failure report that Today shows.
#
# JOB_TIMEOUT is above both gate waits (60 min each) plus both checks, so
# the limit never stops a check that would finish. Mondays at 11:20, when
# the machines are awake.
JOB_SCHEDULE="20 11 * * 1"
JOB_TIMEOUT="4h"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-machine-setup/machine-setup.sh\" doctor gate"
